arch/mips: offer the NaN 2008 choice on generic MIPS32R2

The Q2's userspace ABI is MIPS32R2, o32, hard float with a 64-bit FPU and
IEEE 754-2008 NaNs (docs/vamp-os.md, "Toolchain and libc"). Buildroot ties
MIPS32R2 to legacy NaNs and offers the choice only on R5, so this lets the
generic MIPS32R2 variant pick 2008 too; legacy stays its default, and the
XBurst and interAptiv variants are unchanged.

--- a/arch/Config.in.mips
+++ b/arch/Config.in.mips
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 	select BR2_MIPS_NAN_LEGACY
 config BR2_MIPS_CPU_MIPS32R2
 	bool
-	select BR2_MIPS_NAN_LEGACY
+	select BR2_MIPS_NAN_LEGACY if !BR2_mips_32r2
 config BR2_MIPS_CPU_MIPS32R3
 	bool
 	select BR2_MIPS_NAN_LEGACY
@@ -210,8 +210,9 @@
 
 choice
 	prompt "Target NaN"
+	default BR2_MIPS_ENABLE_NAN_LEGACY if BR2_mips_32r2
 	default BR2_MIPS_ENABLE_NAN_2008
-	depends on BR2_mips_32r5 || BR2_mips_64r5
+	depends on BR2_mips_32r2 || BR2_mips_32r5 || BR2_mips_64r5
 	help
 	  MIPS supports two different NaN encodings, legacy and 2008.
 	  Information about MIPS NaN encodings can be found here:
